From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:52:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/49] feat(cli): -parallel N backs up several directories at
 once (issue #6)

backup_parallel runs up to N directories of a multi-directory run at the same
time, each in its own backup group and PBS session. With VSS, one snapshot
set covering every directory is taken first: concurrent snapshot creations
collide, and the VSS-busy recovery deletes every shadow copy. No upper limit;
the help shows the recommended value (CPUs / 4). "parallel" in the JSON
config. e2e test 10: two directories in parallel with -exclude and
-exclude-from, restored with the official client.
